    devotional: "Emmanuel — God with us. There is no deeper comfort in all of Scripture than these three words. God did not send a messenger or an angel to stand with His people in their need. He came Himself, in the person of His eternal Son, taking on our nature and dwelling among us. The Creator of the universe wrapped Himself in human flesh and walked the roads of Galilee. This is the mystery of the Incarnation.\n\nLet us observe what the name Emmanuel means for our daily life. It means we are never alone. In sorrow, in temptation, in the valley of the shadow — God is with us in Christ. Reader, if you know Jesus Christ by faith, you have God Himself as your companion. What comfort is sufficient to match this? Let Emmanuel be your meditation today.",
