    devotional: "The wise men came from the east seeking Christ, and their journey teaches us lessons we ought never to forget. They came at great cost and great distance. They came in humility, asking rather than declaring. And above all, they came with one object: to worship. They did not come to observe or to debate — they came to fall down before the King.\n\nLet us learn from these men. The truly wise in every age are those who seek Christ above all things and count no sacrifice too great to find Him. Many in Jerusalem knew the prophecies and could have joined the Magi — but they stayed home. Reader, beware the besetting sin of knowing the truth about Christ while never truly seeking Him. The star still shines. Follow it to worship.",
