    devotional: "God's ways are not our ways. The Messiah, the promised King, is driven as a refugee into a foreign land. His parents flee by night like criminals. Every circumstance seems to contradict the promises. And yet in all this we see the hand of a sovereign God, fulfilling Scripture to the letter: Out of Egypt have I called my son. Providence governs even the flights of the night.\n\nLet us take comfort from this passage when our own circumstances seem to contradict God's promises. The road to glory often runs through Egypt. Trials and displacements do not mean God has forgotten His purposes — they are often the very means by which He accomplishes them. Reader, trust God in the darkness of your providences. He who brought His Son safely out of Egypt will bring His people safely home.",
